Share-alike (CC BY-SA / AGPL) means derivatives of the data and code must stay open and
attributed: a fork cannot close what it took, and improvements can flow back. Attribution
in all cases: cite the author and the relevant DOI (see CITATION.cff).

Contributions: by submitting a contribution you agree it is offered under the licence of the
component it touches, and (for data/code) under a Contributor License Agreement permitting the
maintainer to also offer commercial licences. See docs/07_licenciamento.md.

The registry registers evidence; it does not arbitrate truth and is NOT medical advice.
Claims do not replace clinical judgment.

NO WARRANTY. The materials are provided "as is", without warranty of any kind, to the extent
permitted by the applicable licence above.
